      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3e81b5a1-4be4-59c8-84d4-3e8a7a65f83a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Doomquest\n- People: David Michelinie, Bob Layton, John Romita Jr., Doctor Doom, Cynthia Von Doom\n- Companies: Marvel Comics\n- Organizations: Fantastic Four\n- Places: Latveria\n- Concepts: Iron Man rogues gallery\n\nFacts:\n- Doomquest is a two-issue Iron Man story arc written by David Michelinie and Bob Layton, illustrated by John Romita Jr., and published by Marvel Comics.\n- Doomquest is one of the most popular Iron Man stories and establishes Doctor Doom as a member of Iron Man's rogues gallery.\n- Doctor Doom is portrayed in Doomquest as a villainous counterpart to Iron Man who mirrors the superhero's wealth, power armor, and engineering skill.\n- Doctor Doom is the son of the Romani witch Cynthia Von Doom.\n- Doctor Doom has traditionally been the archenemy of the Fantastic Four and the leader of the fictional nation of Latveria.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5a6e08f6-2f0f-5eef-b4bb-85c89e09e1fb",
        "text": "Page: Doomquest. Sentence: \"Doomquest\" is a two-issue Iron Man story arc written by David Michelinie and Bob Layton with art by John Romita Jr. and published by Marvel Comics.\nPage: Doomquest. Sentence: One of the most popular stories of the title character, it establishes Doctor Doom as a member of his rogues gallery, a villainous counterpart who mirrors the superhero with his wealth, power armor and engineering skill.\nPage: Doctor Doom. Sentence: The son of Romani witch Cynthia Von Doom, Doctor Doom traditionally has been the archenemy of the Fantastic Four, and the leader of the fictional nation of Latveria.",
